Fix a soundness issue in the allocation of function values: a function value counted as allocated in any heap in which its reads frame was allocated, though it may capture an object it does not read (`() => n` reads nothing and returns `n`), and allocation is monotone along heap succession, so a function value could be allocated before an object it captures or its reads frame grows to, which proved false. A function value is now allocated where what it captures is: a lambda where its free variables, `this` and the heaps it uses are, and a function handle where its receiver and, for a two-state function, its previous heap are. Its reads frame and results are allocated there, as before.
